  You don't have to recharge the wand, just 'z'ap it repeatedly until
you've wrested the final charge.  'z'ap it once, then hold <ctrl-a> to
repeat.  Be sure you freeze the water squares adjacent to the target
square as well.  Note that wresting one last charge from the /oCold may
not freeze all three of the squares you need to affect.

  Digging down into a frozen/boulder-filled square only to have it flood
would be disheartening.

>and my stuff should come up to the surface, right?  

  No, only invocation items and the "oY would pop to the surface.
You'll have to dig down to your stuff.  If there are unfrozen adjacent
water squares the pit you just dug may reflood.  So be sure to freeze
both adjacent squares.

  Then you'll need to pick up everything except the bag of holding, and
zap a wand of cancellation (probably down: '>') at the BoH to uncurse
it.  There is no other way to uncurse the BoH on the ground besides
wand/spell of cancellation.  As a barbarian the spell of cancellation
seems unlikely to be possible.  


  Have holy water handy to immediately bless the BoH when you pick it
up.  (You don't want the RNG to recurse it immediately with a nastily
timed malignant aura.)



