   No.  Stop, take a deep breath, and just relax for a while.  You're
still thinking about ascending when you should be totally focussed on 
recovering your equipment.

   First, work on turning the target square and adjacent moat squares
into ice or dry land.  Frost horn, wand of cold, spell of cone of cold
(unlikely for a Barbarian), scroll of earth, giant-dropped boulders,
handy boulders already on the level will help here.  

   Poly/polycontrol could let you polymorph into an amphibious monster,
but a monster with a ranged cold attack (to freeze the moat) would
probably be better.  Winter wolf should be guaranteed, possibly white(?)
dragon.  (Double check, eh?)  Then use #monster command after polying.

  Or just hang out on the level, waiting for giants, winter wolves,
white dragons, or death drops of ?oEarth, /oCold, frost horn,
/oCancellation, etc.  If by some miracle you get giants, kill them in a
place that lets you make full use of any boulders they might be
carrying.  

  If you get a monster with a ranged cold attack, do NOT kill it.
Maneuver it so that it eventually freezes all three water squares for
you.  Remember that monsters won't use their ranged attacks when they're
adjacent to you.


   Method of digging down then becomes necessary.  Wand of digging,
non-cursed pick-axe, non-cursed dwarvish mattock, etc.

   The one item you have to have right now is a wand of cancellation.
If the only ones you know about are above Medusa, do you have a way to
controlled levelport?  Or a cursed potion of gain level?


